      "content": "Your frustration highlights a very real disconnect where corporate efficiency metrics often overshadow human value, and it is painful to feel valued only for what you can automate. However, viewing yourself as a \"bug in the code\" overlooks how human experts increasingly serve as essential trainers, ethics auditors, and creative directors for these very systems. The transition to AI does not erase human worth; rather, it shifts the market from demanding pure labor skills to valuing the strategic insight and complex problem-solving that a thirty-year journey naturally provides.",
      "source": "target",
